        "Scan one line and watch the metre work. The curfew tolls the knell of parting day carries five iambs, so it is iambic pentameter, and the beat lands on tolls and knell where grief sits. Gray then lets the stanza's alternating rhyme close each thought. A student who can mark that pattern can explain why a broken line elsewhere feels jagged: the departure from metre is audible only against the rule, which is why scanning is set work in {S}.",
